  (text "R45: each module pulls SLP up with about 100k; 2.2k against seven in parallel holds the line near 0.4 V until the firmware drives IO42." (at 492 188 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left)) (uuid "25045122-5866-4d95-9599-376c54ef0e01"))
  (text "Quadrature counters: one LS7366R per channel on SPI2 (x4, 32-bit, free running; pin numbers from the LS7366R datasheet of June 2014; SPI at 4 MHz, the chip's limit at 3.3 V)." (at 590 22 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left)) (uuid "83fe16c8-b2a6-4dab-bfed-ce27386caef3"))
  (text "A/B from the conditioning rows, INDEX from the channel's switch line (the count can be latched in silicon at the switch edge once the index" (at 590 26 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left)) (uuid "2c32c02c-02a7-42e9-88d8-352d8e1af132"))
  (text "polarity is confirmed; until then the firmware latches by reading CNTR after the expander interrupt). fCKi = CNT_CLK, 4 MHz from the S3. CNT_EN high." (at 590 30 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left)) (uuid "7d0fd2ef-b945-410f-980e-9b4bd9be1795"))
